<overview>
<p>Motorized infantry platoons use light ground vehicles, typically motorcycles or utility trucks, for rapid movement between positions. Faster than foot infantry and cheaper than fully mechanized formations, motorized platoons fill the gap between static garrison troops and armored combat units. They excel at road-bound patrol routes, rapid redeployment along prepared axes, and screening operations where speed matters more than protection. Off-road performance depends heavily on terrain and vehicle type, and the troops must dismount to fight, leaving their transport vulnerable.</p><p>Towing assault-class LB-X autocannon that can fire cluster rounds capable of shredding virtually any target, these field gun crews deliver the heaviest area-effect direct fire available to ground forces. Ballistic plate personal armor helps improve the chances of surviving close contact with opposing forces.</p>
</overview>

<notes>
Intro date selected as common date for LBX20 field gun. Ballistic plate armor chosen for heavy close-contact potential. Full complement of long arms selected due to low field gun ammo.
</notes>

